{"id":"effetto","lemma":"effetto","pos":"noun","rank":753,"glosses":["effect (in all senses)","appearance, show (the way something looks out)","impression, sensation"],"ipa":"/efˈfɛt.to/","gender":"m","forms":{"plural":"effetti"},"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dd/LL-Q652_%28ita%29-DiplomaticBadger-effetto.wav","examples":[{"text":"Che effetto avrà?","en":"What effect will that have?","words":[{"g":"that / what"},null,{"g":"to have","l":"avere"}]},{"text":"In effetti è vero.","en":"As a matter of fact, it is true.","words":[{"g":"in"},null,{"g":"is","l":"essere"},{"g":"true"}]},{"text":"Ci saranno effetti permanenti?","en":"Will there be permanent effects?","words":[{"g":"us / there"},{"g":"to be","l":"essere"},null,{"g":"permanent","l":"permanente"}]},{"text":"La medicina ha fatto effetto.","en":"The medicine took effect.","words":[{"g":"the / her"},{"g":"medicine"},{"g":"has","l":"avere"},{"g":"to do","l":"fare"},null]},{"text":"Gli effetti sono reversibili.","en":"The effects are reversible.","words":[{"g":"the / to him"},null,{"g":"am / are","l":"essere"},null]}]}